      <div class="part-eyebrow"><i data-lucide="map" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true"></i>Part 5</div>
      <h2 id="h-nearterm">What Comes First — The Near-Term Build Plan</h2>
      <p>Vinifera is built in phases. Build one complete, working slice of the product. Verify it against real use. Then build the next slice on top of it. This approach is faster, more reliable, and less risky than building all thirteen modules in parallel and hoping they integrate correctly on the day of release.</p>

      <div class="timeline" aria-label="Build phases">
        <div class="phase phase-current">
          <div class="phase-line">
            <div class="phase-dot" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
            <div class="phase-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="phase-content">
            <span class="phase-tag">Weeks 1–6 &middot; Active</span>
            <h3>The Foundation</h3>
            <p>Secure staff login, magic-link member login, multi-tenant organization architecture, and Stripe subscription billing. No wine club features yet — getting the infrastructure correct before any club features exist is what prevents costly rewrites later.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="phase phase-current">
          <div class="phase-line">
            <div class="phase-dot" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
            <div class="phase-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="phase-content">
            <span class="phase-tag">Weeks 7–16 &middot; Critical</span>
            <h3>The Core Club Loop</h3>
            <p>Member management, club tier configuration, release scheduling, Stripe billing for shipments, payment decline recovery, shipping label generation, and CSV migration import. <strong>Exit criterion:</strong> one real winery adds ten members, creates a release, charges them via Stripe, generates labels, and marks shipments complete. The money moves. The wine ships.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <p><strong>Why two phases before any AI or analytics?</strong> Every other feature depends on real member behavioral data accumulated through real club releases. Building analytics before any winery has processed a real release produces analytics with no data to analyze.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

